entry.summary:
A retry policy can look reasonable on its own and still be impossible inside the request that owns it.
Suppose one provider attempt may take 800 milliseconds. The call allows four attempts with increasing backoff, while the request has two seconds left. The individual numbers are valid, yet the composition cannot fit.
@workit/core/time-policy evaluates that shape before task execution:
import { planTimePolicy } from "@workit/core/time-policy";

const plan = planTimePolicy({
  type: "timeout",
  timeout: "2s",
  policy: {
    type: "retry",
    attempt: {
      type: "attempt",
      duration: "800ms",
    },
    retry: {
      times: 4,
      initialDelay: "100ms",
      factor: 2,
      jitter: false,
    },
  },
});

if (!plan.valid) {
  console.error(plan.warnings);
}

